# %ECSV 1.0
# ---
# datatype:
# - {name: id, datatype: string, description: stable identifier used in configs}
# - {name: label, datatype: string}
# - {name: species, datatype: string}
# - {name: kind, datatype: string, description: 'line: narrow feature (edges = +/- width); band: broad feature (edges as given)'}
# - {name: wavelength_um, unit: um, datatype: float64, description: central (vacuum) wavelength; NaN for bands with no single centre}
# - {name: wave_min_um, unit: um, datatype: float64, description: lower edge used when masking/selecting the feature}
# - {name: wave_max_um, unit: um, datatype: float64, description: upper edge used when masking/selecting the feature}
# - {name: transition, datatype: string}
# - {name: source, datatype: string}
# - {name: notes, datatype: string}
# meta: !!omap
# - {dataset: gas_lines}
# - {description: 'Atomic and molecular gas-phase lines/bands in the 1-28 um range commonly seen with NIRSpec and MIRI, including the
#     molecular inventory of inner protoplanetary disks reported by JWST'}
# - {version: 2026.08.1}
# - {provenance: Compiled for jwstflow from the references below; wavelengths are vacuum values as commonly quoted in the JWST literature.
#     Verify against the primary source before line-precise work.}
# - references: ['Roueff et al. 2019, A&A 630, A58 (H2 line list)', NIST ASD (Kramida et al.); fine-structure lines, 'Hydrogen recombination
#       lines (vacuum), e.g. van Hoof 2018', HITRAN2020 (Gordon et al. 2022), Tabone et al. 2023 (soot line; C4H2 and C6H6) and Arabhavi
#       et al. 2024 (hydrocarbon-rich VLMS disks), 'Grant et al. 2023, ApJL 947, L6 (13CO2 detection)', 'Banzatti et al. 2023, 2025 (JWST-MIRI
#       water excitation atlas)', Tabone et al. 2021 and Zannese et al. 2024 (OH prompt emission), 'Henning et al. 2024, PASP 136, 054302
#       (MINDS overview)']
# - {notes: For narrow lines a mask half-width of `line_width_um` or n resolution elements is applied by the consuming step.}
# - {usage: 'Select in a workflow with `features: {<dataset>: all | [ids or species]}` or a list of ids.'}
# schema: astropy-2.0
id label species kind wavelength_um wave_min_um wave_max_um transition source notes
h2_0-0_s0 "H2 0-0 S(0)" H2 line 28.2188 nan nan "v=0-0 S(0)" "Roueff et al. 2019, A&A 630, A58 (H2 line list)" "beyond MRS ch4 nominal range"
